STEP 1: Create a folder named myapp on Desktop.

STEP 2: Create index.html

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>My App</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to My App</h1>
    <p>This is my first Docker application.</p>
</body>
</html>

STEP 3: Create a file named Dockerfile (without extension)

FROM tomcat:10.1-jdk17-temurin
RUN mkdir -p /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/myapp
COPY index.html /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/myapp/index.html
EXPOSE 8080

STEP 4: Open CMD inside the myapp folder and execute:

docker build -t my-tomcat .
docker images
docker run -d --name my-tomcat-container -p 8080:8080 my-tomcat

STEP 5: Open in browser:
http://localhost:8080/myapp/

STEP 6: Stop the container:

docker stop my-tomcat-container

STEP 7: Push image to Docker Hub:

docker login
docker tag my-tomcat YOUR_USERNAME/my-tomcat:latest
docker push YOUR_USERNAME/my-tomcat:latest
